# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What must never enter a commit.
#
# This file is written defensively rather than minimally. Two of the entries
# below exist because something nearly went wrong, and they are marked as such:
# an ignore rule is only worth as much as the filename you thought of in
# advance, so the categories are deliberately wider than this project's own
# habits. `scripts/hooks/pre-commit` is the second line of defence, for the
# filenames nobody thought of.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Dependencies and build output -----------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
web/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Every .env variant, including backups and copies. A narrow `.env` rule once
# let a `.env.backup-before-rename` into a commit; `.env*` is the fix. The
# second line catches the OTHER spelling -- prod.env, secrets.env -- which the
# first one does not match, because `.env*` only anchors the leading dot.
.env*
!.env.example
*.env

# Keys, certificates and credential stores of every shape. Nothing here should
# ever exist in this repo; that is exactly why it is cheap to exclude.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*.gpg
*.asc
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# Tunnel and deployment credentials -- zrok, ngrok and cloudflared all write
# tokens to disk, and this project has used all three.
.zrok/
.ngrok*
*.tunnel.json
cloudflared*.json

# --- Archives --------------------------------------------------------------
# THE NEAR-MISS. Building a source tarball at the repo root sweeps up
# `server/.env` unless you remember to exclude it, and a secret inside a
# .tgz is invisible to every text-based secret scan -- including the ones run
# on this repo. Only a manual `rm` kept one out of a `git add -A`. Archives are
# build artefacts or transfers; neither belongs in version control.
*.tgz
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.gz

# --- Databases -------------------------------------------------------------
# KIRANA_DB is configurable, so the database does not always land in
# server/data/ -- and SQLite's WAL and shared-memory sidecars are separate
# files that carry the same rows.
server/data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.dump
*.sql

# --- Logs and crash output -------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
report.*.json

# --- Generated demo artefacts ----------------------------------------------
artifacts/*
!artifacts/.gitkeep

# --- Editors, tools and operating systems ----------------------------------
# .vscode/ is deliberately NOT ignored: launch.json and tasks.json are how a
# reviewer runs this project, and both were checked for secrets. The local
# settings files that tools write per-machine are excluded.
.vscode/*.local.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.claude/settings.local.json

# Third-party agent skills, installed locally so the design and review passes
# have something to check against. They are somebody else's work and say
# nothing about this project, so they stay out of a repo that is being read
# to judge this one. Reinstall from their upstream repos; nothing here
# depends on them at build or run time.
.claude/skills/

# The desktop app drops files it hands you into a folder here. They are working
# documents -- drafts, scripts, notes -- not part of the project.
Claude outputs/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
